\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 Chairman\rquote s Report
\par }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 A whole legend grew up around the simple expression }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid7278522 \'93Somewhere in France\'94}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 
. This was of course how British soldiers writing home in the Great War sati}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2446142 sfied the censors by concealing}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818  their unit\rquote 
s current geographical position on the battlefield. In much happier circumstances the Paris Branch can now declare openly that we are owners of a new Clubhouse not only }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid7278522 \'93Somewhere in France\'94}{
\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2446142 , but we can be }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 precise: 28, rue des Acacias, 75017 Paris  We are keeping our old telephone number:  01.47.42.19.26, and we expect 
to be reconnected in the week of Monday 12}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\super\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 th}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818  October.
\par You will sense the feeling of relief in our Secretary\rquote }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2446142 s Report attached}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 
, that we are at last coming up the finishing straight. For the Branch archives it will be worth recording here the story of how we }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2446142 came to move after 81 years at r}{
\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 ue Boudreau.  It is a story of dedicated}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2446142  team-work, so that telling the}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 
 story will give us the opportunity to thank all those who gave so liberally of their time. Of course I do so at the risk that someone\rquote s name will be omitted and if so I apologize in advance.  It began with the findings of a working party}{
\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid7278522 ,}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818  chaired by David Edwards}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid7278522 ,}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 
 which was set }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid7278522 up to propose a Business Plan on}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818  the future direction}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2446142 
 the Paris Branch should take. }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 David Bean, Charles Spencer-Barnard and Nic
holas Harding sat on this Working Party. Inevitably they found themselves up against a brick wall: our premises no longer met new Health and Safety regulations, and to carry out the necessary work to bring us into line would cost an estimated 100,000 euro
s}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid7278522 .  Not possessing those funds }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 
we arrived  at the painful conclusion that we had to relocate. The baton was now passed to our Property Member Charles Spencer-Ba}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid7278522 rnard. After a few unsuitable}{
\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818  properties had been visited Joan Hicks contacted our member Mad
ame Desaintjean, whose nephew, a Paris estate agent, proposed to us the property at the rue des Acacias. Charles visited this address and recommended to your Committee that it met the search criteria.  Our House Manager, David Bean, then took the project 
in hand, and with extraordinary attention to detail arrived at a definition of what works would be required to give us a result of which the Branch could be proud. Our sale and purchase transactions were not back-to-back. We }{
\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 first }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 sold 8, rue Boudreau to the Mais
on du Limousin, our neighbours in the building, who kindly allowed us to store our chattels and hold our Committee meetings until we found a new Clubhouse. On purchasing 28, rue des Acacias we gave a mandate to a main contractor for the necessary works to
 be carried out. In the critical month of August there was a slippage of three weeks before they had agreed terms with the}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2446142 ir}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 
 sub-contractors. This held up the project considerably. Meanwhile the Maison du Limousin needed the space at rue Boudreau so that a working party consisting of David and Swee Ching Edwards and Liz Thorn supervised the removal of our chattels to r}{
\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2446142 ue des Acacias, where they }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 had}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2446142  to be stored in our cave and in that}{
\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818  of the Concierge. As soon as the Clubhouse was ready to recei
ve selected items from storage another working party including David Portsmouth and Tony Bennett brought those selected items up to ground level again}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2446142 , moving the remainder into the Concierge\rquote 
s cave, thus liberating our own cave for upgrading work}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 .  Throughout the whole episode the invaluable contribution of your vigilant Branch Secretary and Treasure
r needs to be mentioned. Without their readiness to pick up the baton and run with it when required the project would have been impossible to manage. Finally a vote of thanks to our House Manager, David Bean, for his massive contribution in project manage
ment during the formative stages. He has now stepped down as House Manger and he can}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818  }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid7278522 look back on his}{
\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818  }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid7278522 work }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid15952818 with a deep sense of satisfaction.
\par Thank you all Ladies and Gentlemen. Now we can look to the future in the best of conditions. So do please put t
he word around that the Royal British Legion is alive and kicking and keen to attract new members.  Your Committee will be formulating a Membership drive strategy.
